==English==
[[Image:Borage-flower-hr.jpg|thumb|''Borago officinalis'']]

===Etymology===
{{bor|en|fro|borage}} (compare {{cog|fr|bourrache}}), from {{der|en|ML.|borrago}}, either from {{der|en|la|borra|t=short wool, rough hair}} or {{der|en|ar|الأب من العرق|tr=abu min arak|lit=father of sweat}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbɒɹ.ɪdʒ/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{taxlink|Borago officinalis|species|noshow=1}}, a [[Mediterranean]] [[plant]] with rough, cucumber-flavored leaves, used in [[salad]]s.

